    <name>
      <text>Directional Derivatives_Number 1</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider the function \(f(x,y)\) given below,</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle f(x,y)={@func@}\)</p>  
<p>Calculate the gradient function \(\nabla f (x,y)\) </p>
<p>\(\nabla f (x,y)=\) \(\displaystyle ( \) [[input:ans1]]\(,\)[[input:ans2]]\(\displaystyle ) \)</p>
<p>[[validation:ans1]][[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt1]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p>What we need to do here is to find \(\displaystyle \frac{d}{dy}f(x,y)\) and \(\displaystyle \frac{d}{dx}f(x,y)\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{d}{dx}f(x,y)={@gradient_func1@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle\frac{d}{dy}f(x,y)={@gradient_func2@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \nabla f (x,y)={@gradient_func1@},{@gradient_func2@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
